  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Pat the cod dry with paper towels.",
    "In a 9x13 inch baking dish, toss the tomatoes with 2 tbsp olive oil, the garlic, olives, capers, oregano, red pepper flakes, and 1/4 tsp salt.",
    "Roast the tomatoes for 8 minutes, until they start to soften and split.",
    "Rub the cod with the remaining 1 tbsp olive oil. Season both sides with the remaining 1/2 tsp salt and the black pepper.",
    "Nestle the fillets into the tomatoes and spoon some of the tomatoes over the top.",
    "Bake for 10 to 12 minutes, until the fish is opaque and flakes easily and reads 145 F in the thickest part.",
    "Squeeze 2 lemon wedges over the dish and scatter with parsley. Serve with the remaining wedges and the pan juices."
  ],
